<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>

<!-- PLUGIN DEFINITIONS -->
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "sanoid">
<!ENTITY author "andrebrait">
<!ENTITY version "2026.11.11">
<!ENTITY repo "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andrebrait/unraid-sanoid/master">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "&repo;/&name;.plg">
  <!ENTITY plugin    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
  <!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN  name="&name;"
     author="&author;"
     version="&version;"
     pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
     support="https://github.com/andrebrait/unraid-sanoid/issues"
     min="7.0.0"
>

<CHANGES>

###2026.11.11
Installs Sanoid 2.3.0 (https://github.com/jimsalterjrs/sanoid/releases/tag/v2.3.0) with these upstream fixes that are not in a release yet:
- syncoid escapes ZFS resume tokens, so a malicious remote receiver can no longer inject commands on the sender (pull request 1114, fixing issue 1118)
- sanoid no longer loses snapshot cache entries after a zfs-recursive snapshot (recursive = zfs), which made it take extra snapshots (pull request 1023)
- sanoid no longer prints cache updates to the console, which made cron send mail (pull request 1071)

The plugin is now a maintained fork named Sanoid, by andrebrait, based on steini84's unRAID6-Sanoid plugin. Installing it removes the unRAID6-Sanoid plugin.
Support: https://github.com/andrebrait/unraid-sanoid/issues
The Sanoid package is built from the SHA256-verified upstream release by a GitHub Actions workflow in this repository, instead of a prebuilt binary of unknown origin.
The plugin requires Unraid 7.0 or newer; support for Unraid 6 and its extra mbuffer and perl packages was removed.
The plugin is versioned by release date; each entry names the Sanoid version it installs.
Fixed the post-install message: Sanoid is installed at /usr/local/sbin/sanoid, not /usr/local/bin/sanoid.

###2025.10.21
Update to Sanoid 2.3.0
https://github.com/jimsalterjrs/sanoid/releases/tag/v2.3.0

###2024.07.15
Do not install perl package on unraid 6.11.0 or later

###2024.07.11
Do not install mbuffer and perl package on unraid 7

###2024.04.30
New version of mbuffer fixed - mbuffer-20240107-x86_64-1_SBo.tgz (compiled by @SoerenS from https://slackbuilds.org/repository/15.0/system/mbuffer/)

###2023.07.26
New version of mbuffer fixed

###2023.07.20
Update to Sanoid 2.2.0 and dependencies (mbuffer and  perl)
https://github.com/jimsalterjrs/sanoid/releases/tag/v2.2.0

###2021.04.03
Update to Sanoid 2.1.0
https://github.com/jimsalterjrs/sanoid/releases/tag/v2.1.0

###2020.10.07
Initial release Sanoid 2.0.3


</CHANGES>

<!-- The plugin manager does not overwrite existing files, so remove the description before writing the current one. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
rm -f &emhttp;/README.md
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/README.md">
<INLINE>
**Sanoid**

Sanoid is a policy-driven snapshot management tool for ZFS filesystems. Based on steini84's Sanoid plugin.

</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/&name;.png" Type="base64">
<INLINE>

</INLINE>
</FILE>

